00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.840
the average number of hours you need to
get 40 joules per square centimeter

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.789
of light on your skin from a screen is

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:16.200
somewhere around fifteen to thirty days
there's a bit of a catch here when we're

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.520
comparing these times screens tend to
produce more of the shorter wavelengths

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.540
of light that cause more damage than the
